/-!
# The topos of a fibred category over a ringed site

Let `(D, O_D)` be a ringed site and let `p : C ⥤ D` be a fibred category. Give `C` the topology
inherited from `D` (Stacks 06NV): a family of morphisms of `C` covers when each member is
strongly cartesian over its image and the family of images covers in `D`. The projection `p` is
then continuous and cocontinuous for that topology, so it induces a morphism of topoi
`π : Sh(C) ⟶ Sh(D)` whose inverse image is restriction along `p.op` and whose direct image is
the right adjoint of that restriction.

This file sets up the site, the two (co)continuity statements and that morphism of topoi, and
records the base ringed site as a ringed topos in the universe in which `π` is formed.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.FibredCategorySituation`: the standing data, a ringed site
  together with a fibred category over its underlying site.
* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.FibredCategorySituation.topology`: the inherited topology on the
  total category.
* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.FibredCategorySituation.ProjectionData` and
  `inducedProjection`: the morphism of topoi induced by the projection, specified by both of
  its canonical functors and their adjunction;
  `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.FibredCategorySituation.projection` is the morphism itself.
* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.FibredCategorySituation.liftedBaseSheaf`: the base structure
  sheaf with its sections lifted to the universe in which `π` is formed, and
  `baseRingedTopos`: the base, as a ringed topos in that universe.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.isSheafFor_functorPullback_of_isFibered`: for a fibred `p`, if a
  presheaf on `D` is a sheaf for a sieve `B` on `p.obj X`, then its restriction along `p.op` is
  a sheaf for the functor pullback of `B` to `X`. This is the sheaf-theoretic content of
  continuity.
* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.isContinuous_inheritedTopology_of_isFibered` and
  `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.isCocontinuous_inheritedTopology_of_isFibered`: the projection of
  a fibred category is continuous and cocontinuous from the inherited topology to the base
  topology.
* `Stacks.Sites.FibredCategory.generate_mem_iff_map_generate`: a morphism lies in the sieve
  generated by a presieve of strongly cartesian morphisms exactly when its image lies in the
  sieve generated by the image presieve.
* `CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp_forget_commRingCat`: a presheaf of
  commutative rings whose underlying presheaf of sets is a sheaf is a sheaf, with the universe
  of the site unrelated to the universe of the rings.

## Implementation notes

**How the tag is split.** Stacks 08P8 is a *Situation* with four clauses: the standing data,
the associated morphism of topoi, the structure sheaf `O_C = π⁻¹ O_D`, and the assertion that
`π` is thereby a morphism of *ringed* topoi. The first two are here, on
`FibredCategorySituation` and `inducedProjection`. The last two need the inverse image of a
sheaf of *commutative* rings along a morphism of topoi, so they live on
`FibredCategorySituation.totalRingedTopos` and `ringedProjection`, in the module that imports
that functor; together the four declarations are the tag's covering set.

**The continuity statements are not specializations of Stacks 06NW.**
`CategoryTheory.Functor.IsFibredOneMorphism.isContinuous_and_isCocontinuous_inheritedTopology`
proves both conjuncts for a 1-morphism of fibred categories, and taking the second structure
functor to be `𝟭 D` and the 1-morphism to be `p` is the case at hand — but that form needs
`HasPullbacks D` and speaks of `(𝟭 D).inheritedTopology J` rather than of `J` itself. The two
lemmas below need neither, so they are proved directly rather than derived.

**The morphism of topoi is packaged as data with equations.** `ProjectionData` carries the
morphism of topoi together with the identification of its inverse image with
`sheafPushforwardContinuous`, of its direct image with `sheafPushforwardCocontinuous`, and of
its adjunction with `sheafAdjunctionCocontinuous`. This pins the maps the source names rather
than asserting that some morphism of topoi exists. The adjunction is compared with `HEq`,
because its type mentions the two functors which the preceding equations identify.

**The value universe.** The topoi are formed in `Type (max w uD vD uC vC)`, large enough for
both sites and for the sections of `O_D`, so that the right adjoint of restriction exists. The
base structure sheaf is transported there by `liftedBaseSheaf`, which is `ULift` on sections;
that it is still a sheaf is `Presieve.isSheaf_comp_uliftFunctor_iff` together with
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isSheaf_of_isSheaf_comp_forget_commRingCat`.

